      "19302": {
        "comments": [
          {
            "text": "Created attachment 4035\nPatch\n\nSince https://svn.r-project.org/browse/R?rev=87565, `save()` allows saving `.rda` files with zstd compression.\n\nHowever:\n\n- `checkRdaFiles()` reports compression as `\"unknown\"` for these files\n- `\"zstd\"` is not exposed as an option in `resaveRdaFiles()`\n\n```\ntest_rda <- tempfile(fileext = \".rda\")\n\nsave(mtcars, file = test_rda, compress = \"zstd\")\n\ntools::checkRdaFiles(test_rda)\n#>                                       size ASCII compress version\n#> /tmp/RtmpWVb0sy/file3af8f42b18f43.rda 1266 FALSE  unknown       3\n```\n\nAttached is a minimal patch to expand support for zstd compression for Rda files to these 2 functions.\n\nI didn't want to make any major design decision in the initial patch but it probably makes sense to add a bias in favour of zstd in `resaveRdaFiles()`, the same way there is currently a bias towards gzip, since zstd generally allows much faster compression/decompression than other algorithms (xz in particular).",
            "bug_id": 19302,
            "count": 0,
            "creation_time": "2026-11-12T15:53:34Z",
            "id": 104185,
            "is_private": false,
            "tags": [],
            "is_markdown": true,
            "creator": "hugo.gruson+Rbugzilla",
            "time": "2026-11-12T15:53:34Z",
            "attachment_id": 4035
          },
          {
            "creator": "ikrylov",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-21T19:52:59Z",
            "text": "Created attachment 4139\nExpanded patch\n\nThank you for the report and the patch!\n\nThis has implications for CRAN. Zstandard support appeared in R-4.5.0 and will be required in R-4.7.0, so `R CMD build` will need to add at least `Depends: R (>= 4.5.0)` when building packages with zstd-compressed data, and R CMD check will need to test for that the same way it currently tests for `Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)` for packages containing version-3 serialised data. Attaching a more involved patch based on your proposal.\n\nTo test:\n\n```\nsetwd(tempdir())\npackage.skeleton('foo', list = character())\ndir.create('foo/data')\nsaveRDS('v3', 'foo/v3.rds', version = 3)\nsaveRDS('zst', 'foo/zst.rds', version = 2, compress = 'zstd')\naa <- rep(volcano, 0xaa)\n# couldn't find an example where zstd would win under --resave-data=best\nsave(aa, file = 'foo/data/aa.rda', compress = 'zstd')\ntools::Rcmd('build foo')\n```\n```\n* checking if a ‘data/datalist’ file should be added ... no\n  NB: this package now depends on R (>= 3.5.0)\n  WARNING: Added dependency on R >= 3.5.0 because serialized objects in serialize/load version 3 cannot be read in older versions of R.\n  File(s) containing such objects:\n    ‘foo/v3.rds’\n  NB: this package now depends on R (>= 4.5.0)\n  WARNING: Added dependency on R >= 4.5.0 because zstd-compressed serialized objects cannot be read in older versions of R.\n  File(s) containing such objects:\n    ‘foo/data/aa.rda’ ‘foo/zst.rds’\n```\n```\nuntar('foo_1.0.tar.gz')\ndesc <- as.data.frame(read.dcf('foo/DESCRIPTION'))\ndesc$Depends <- NULL\nwrite.dcf(desc, 'foo/DESCRIPTION')\n# now the package does not depend on R >= 4.5.0\ntar('foo_1.0.tar.gz', 'foo')\nSys.setenv('_R_CHECK_SERIALIZATION_' = 'TRUE')\ntools::Rcmd('check foo_1.0.tar.gz')\n```\n```\n* checking serialization versions ... WARNING\nFound zstd-compressed serialized file(s):\n  ‘data/aa.rda’ ‘zst.rds’\nSuch files are only readable in R >= 4.5.0.\nRecreate them without compress = \"zstd\" or set Depends: R (>= 4.5.0) as appropriate\n WARNING\nFound file(s) with version 3 serialization:\n  ‘v3.rds’\nSuch files are only readable in R >= 3.5.0.\nRecreate them with R < 3.5.0 or save(version = 2) or saveRDS(version = 2) as appropriate\n```\n\nShould `resave_data_others` be also taught to use zstd?\n\nCurrently, no saved or serialised data is zstd-compressed on CRAN, but there are a few `.zst` files in `inst/extdata/` (`pgenlibr`, bundles `libzstd`) and `tests/testthat/fixtures/` (`rmoriedata`).",
            "bug_id": 19302,
            "count": 1,
            "is_markdown": true,
            "attachment_id": 4139,
            "tags": [],
            "time": "2026-11-21T19:52:59Z",
